# █▀ █▀ █░█
# ▄█ ▄█ █▀█
#
# Why: the key stays passphrase-protected on disk; on its first use after
# login ssh adds it to ssh-agent (ssh-agent.service, SSH_AUTH_SOCK in uwsm env
# and zsh 10-env), so the passphrase is asked once per login, not per push.
# No secrets here: the key itself is never tracked (.chezmoiignore).

Host *
    AddKeysToAgent yes
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
